{"chunk_id": "11e68ed3d358", "text": "Lakshmana delivers Rama\u2019s cruel command that Sita must be abandoned, and the shock overwhelms her. Hearing his harsh words, Sita collapses in despair on the banks of the Ganges but soon regains consciousness and laments her fate. She wonders what sin she could have committed to deserve rejection despite her chastity and devotion, recalling how she once followed Rama happily into exile. Now cast off and alone, she asks how she can face the ascetics or explain her disgrace. Though grief-stricken, she refuses suicide for fear of ending the royal line, implying her pregnancy. Accepting the king\u2019s order as unavoidable, she asks Lakshmana to obey Rama but to carry her final message: she is pure and faithful, and Rama has abandoned her only out of fear of public reproach. The passage crystallizes the tragedy of duty versus compassion in the Ramayana.\nLakshmana obeys Rama\u2019s order to abandon Sita by the Ganges, where she laments her fate and asks him to convey her final words to Rama.\nThemes: exile and abandonment, duty vs compassion, royal reputation, Sita's lament, obedience to command", "vector": [0.00423728721216321, -0.024527374655008316, 0.00271620973944664, 0.0022035252768546343, -0.024568118155002594, 0.0197196826338768, -0.026333654299378395, -0.00673959543928504, -0.025382980704307556, -0.021240759640932083, 0.03058452159166336, 0.024921225383877754, 0.0151157071813941, 0.020208600908517838, -0.006756571587175131, -0.00470243813470006, 0.047099076211452484, -0.008888796903192997, 0.0271620973944664, -0.024961967021226883, -0.005731202661991119, -0.018293673172593117, 0.00485182972624898, 0.0072454893961548805, -0.029498038813471794, -0.0165552981197834, 0.018198605626821518, -0.0282757431268692, 0.011930951848626137, -0.013737230561673641, -0.030693169683218002, -0.009588220156729221, -0.019950561225414276, -0.016012055799365044, -0.033681001514196396, 0.0045326752588152885, -0.004271239973604679, -0.0196517780